  "findings": [
    "REJECTED for complete explicit-date formatting: valid checker_format_zone leaves Z z XXX literal; checker_format_width produces 70-01-01 11:00:00 instead of 1970-1-1 11:0:0; checker_format_literal drops the escaped apostrophe in year's day. Each fails exact source and shipped SVG.",
    "Java DateFunction.executeReturnFunction converts seconds with TValue.toInt(), multiplies by 1000L and formats with SimpleDateFormat. Rust uses a partial custom formatter. The formatting defects predate this patch but remain relevant counterexamples to its stated complete output contract.",
    "Positive evidence: nine of twelve new valid canonical cases pass, including signed i32 extrema, midnight and leap/expression boundaries and four DST-instant controls. All twelve supplemental live host-zone comparisons pass across Australia/Melbourne, Asia/Kathmandu and UTC, with no debug timezone override. Thus signed instant/timezone conversion has separate bounded evidence, but this is not acceptance of full date formatting or of the combined stream revision.",
    "Two deliberately invalid controls are preserved outside valid-positive counts: out-of-range epoch seconds yield Java exit 1 and empty stdout; invalid QQ pattern yields Java exit 200 and error SVG. Rust exits 0 for both, silently replacing an invalid timestamp with empty text or passing unknown format tokens through. Empty Java stdout is retained as the empty .svg with stderr, never fabricated or excluded.",
    "No non-Unix runtime was tested; existing UTC fallback is residue. Repair date formatting/error propagation or seek an explicitly narrowed accounted mechanism with a fresh independent review; do not infer that this review approves the isolated date patch.",
    "The maker account uses claimed_invariant/planned_model_change instead of required invariant/planned_change; unchanged schema guard rejects it. Account editing is outside checker ownership."
  ],
